1. Upload the Zip to Lambda
Go to the Lambda Console → select your function (mylambda) or create a new one.

Under Code → Upload from → .zip file, choose projectfunction.zip.

Set the Handler to lambda_function.lambda_handler (assuming your entry function is lambda_handler inside lambda_function.py).

Runtime: Python 3.x.

2. Configure IAM Role
Attach an execution role with:

AWSLambdaBasicExecutionRole (for logs).

DynamoDB access (scoped to your table ContactFormData).

3. DynamoDB Table
Table name: ContactFormData.

Partition key: email (String).

This means every record is keyed by the user’s email.

4. API Gateway Integration
In API Gateway Console, create a resource /contact.

Add a POST method → integrate with your Lambda.

Deploy to stage dev.

Invoke URL will look like:

Code
https://tge4qpx2xe.execute-api.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/dev/contact
5. Frontend Pages
contactus.html → form should POST to the API Gateway endpoint.

success.html → redirect after submission.

⚡ AWS CLI Shortcut (Optional)
If you prefer command line instead of console:

bash
aws lambda update-function-code \
  --function-name mylambda \
  --zip-file fileb://projectfunction.zip
This uploads your zip directly to the Lambda function.
